# Task 01 — Holy Grail Layout

**Category:** Layout & Structure
**Difficulty:** above-average
**Style school:** Minimalism

## The problem

A classic header/sidebar/footer/main layout that must stay solid at every screen
size and with any amount of main content.

## Constraints

- Grid Template Areas only — no Flexbox allowed for the primary layout.
- The footer must stay pinned to the bottom even when main content is short.
- The layout must remain usable on mobile screens, not just desktop.

## Key implementation decisions

- Used Tailwind's arbitrary property syntax (`[grid-template-areas:...]`)
  instead of an inline `style` attribute, since Tailwind v4 has no dedicated
  utility class for naming template areas but does support arbitrary CSS
  properties directly in a class.
- The grid stacks vertically on mobile (`grid-cols-1`, four separate rows: one
  per region) and switches to the classic side-by-side layout from the `md:`
  breakpoint up, using a second, responsive-prefixed arbitrary property for
  `grid-template-areas`.
- Sidebar width is fixed (`200px`) on desktop and the main column takes the
  remaining space (`1fr`), so the layout never breaks when content changes.
- The back-to-home link lives inside the header itself (not `absolute`), so it
  takes up real space in the grid instead of floating over other content.
- Flexbox is still used _inside_ the sidebar nav — the constraint only applies
  to the four main regions, not their internal content.
